.TH MARKDOWN_VIEWER 1
.SH NAME
markdown-viewer \- view markdown files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B markdown-viewer
.IR file[s]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B markdown-viewer
Markdown viewer renders selected parts of the markdown file in an Adwaita
styled window. It automatically updates the rendered content when the file
is changed on disk, so it can be used to preview markdown files while editing
them. It also watches any rendered images for changes and updates them as well.
.PP
The most powerful feature is that it can watch non-markdown files and
on change call a user defined command. This allows previews of files that are
auto-generated from YAML documents (for now). By adding a #!<command> line
to the top of the YAML file this conversion is activated. The command
will substitute the string $INPUT for the path to the YAML file and $OUTPUT
for the path to the generated md file. PlantUML diagrams can also be watched
this way, adding the comment "'!plantuml $INPUT' to the top of the plantuml
file.

